uding other predators, ungulate management outside the park, and weather.","category":"cause","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Changes in wolf predation patterns and impacts on prey species like elk are inextricably linked to other factors, such as other predators, management of ungulates outside the park, and weather (e.g. drought, winter severity).","narrative":"veranderingen in predatie en de effecten op elanden samenvallen met andere factoren, waaronder andere roofdieren, beheer van hoefdieren buiten het park en het weer","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source explicitly links these changes and impacts to the listed factors. “Vallen samen” is more cautious than asserting a single direct cause.","materiality":"Low."},{"excerpt":"Wolven zijn daarmee niet de enige bepalende kracht in dit samenspel.","claim":"Wolves are not the sole determining factor in this interplay.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Consequently, changes in prey selection and kill rates through time result from complex interactions among these factors.","narrative":"niet bij wolven als enige bepalende kracht","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source attributes changing prey selection and kill rates to complex interactions among multiple factors, supporting the conclusion that wolves are not the sole determinant.","materiality":"Low."}]}

